            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "In this study, we present an updated version of the ALARO-0 regional climate model originally introduced by the De Troch et al. (2013), where the surface scheme ISBA is now replaced by the SURFEX (Surface Externalis\u00e9e) scheme (Hamdi et al., 2014). This ALARO model was originally developed for numerical weather prediction (NWP) by the ALADIN consortium\u00b9, which comprised the national (hydro)meteorological services of 16 European and northern African countries (Termonia et al., 2018a). The ALARO model is one of three canonical model configurations (CMCs) within the ALADIN framework, along with the baseline ALADIN model and the AROME model. For a more detailed description, we refer to Termonia et al. (2018a) and to Sect. 2. Moreover, from cycle 40 onwards, ALARO underwent substantial updates, leading to the development of ALARO-1. This new version marked a step-wise change compared to the original ALARO-0.",
